<title>LEBANON: Lebanon gets $7 mln credit to import Syrian oil.</title>
<headline>Lebanon gets $7 mln credit to import Syrian oil.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Arab Trade Fund Programme has provided a $7 million credit to Bank of Beirut to finance imports of Syrian oil, the bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>The agreement was signed by fund chairman Jassim al-Manai and Bank of Beirut chairman Salim Sfeir at the fund headquarters in Abu Dhabi on Thursday, it said.</p>
<p>The fund was set up five years ago by the Abu Dhabi-based Arab Monetary Fund and other regional financial institutions with capital of $500 million to finance trade among Arab countries.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 353078 861723</p>
